    "answer": {
      "short": "$154, 253, 352, 451, 550, 759, 858, 957$.\n\nThe alternating digit sum is $0$ or $11$.",
      "worked": "Let $a$ be the hundreds digit and $b$ the units digit, where $1\\le a\\le9$ and $0\\le b\\le9$. The alternating digit sum is $a-5+b$, which ranges from $-4$ to $13$. Its only possible multiples of $11$ are $0$ and $11$.\n\nIf $a-5+b=0$, then $a+b=5$. The possible pairs $(a,b)$ are $(1,4),(2,3),(3,2),(4,1),(5,0)$, giving $154,253,352,451,550$.\n\nIf $a-5+b=11$, then $a+b=16$. The possible pairs are $(7,9),(8,8),(9,7)$, giving $759,858,957$.\n\nTherefore, all the numbers are $154,253,352,451,550,759,858,957$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
